@startuml
'SD Host Controller Simplified Specification - Shared Bus Control and Clock Pin Selection

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

' Shared Bus Control Register Table
package "Table 2-44: Shared Bus Control Register" {
  rectangle "Register" {
    map "Bits 02-00 | HwInit" {
      Field => Number of Clock Pins
      Description1 => This field indicates support of clock pins to select one\nof devices for shared bus system. Up to 7 clock pins can be supported.
      Description2 => Shared bus is supported by specific system. Then Standard\nHost Driver does not support control of these clock pins.
    }
    
    rectangle "Values" {
      card "000b : Shared bus is not supported"
      card "001b : 1 SDCLK pin is supported"
      card "010b : 2 SDCLK pins are supported"
      card ".... : .........................."
      card "111b : 7 SDCLK pins are supported"
    }
  }
}

' Clock Pin Selection Timing Diagram
rectangle "Figure 2-38: An Example Timing of Selecting Clock Pin" {
  [Clock Pin Select[02:00]] as CPS
  component "000b" as V000
  component "001b" as V001
  component "010b" as V010
  component "011b" as V011
  
  [CLK[1]] as CLK1
  [CLK[2]] as CLK2
  [CLK[3]] as CLK3
  
  note right of CPS
    When Clock Pin Select = 000b: no clocks generated
    When Clock Pin Select = 001b: CLK[1] active (device 1 selected)
    When Clock Pin Select = 010b: CLK[2] active (device 2 selected)
    When Clock Pin Select = 011b: CLK[3] active (device 3 selected)
  end note
}

' Implementation Notes
rectangle "Implementation Notes" {
  note as N1
    Lock-Reset pin is defined by eSD Version 2.10 to improve security level
    for updating boot loader and system codes. The Host System supporting 
    Lock-Reset needs to consider following points:
    
    - Driving Lock-Reset to high during device power off is not allowed
    - Lock-Rest signal can be driven to high after power is supplied
    - Host interface voltage (VDDH) should be always supplied
    - Host System should implement so that VDDH is not controlled by
      SD Bus Power bit in the Power Control register
    
    For eSD:
    - Sleep mode should be used instead of eSD device power off
    - Memory voltage VDDF can be off when device is in Sleep State
    
    For SDIO:
    - Embedded SDIO can support back-end function power pin
    - The back-end function power can be off while IOEx=0
  end note
}

@enduml